  ]\;

## MSYS2

MSYS2 tree for `opam init --cygwin-local-install --cygwin-location=<obj>` in
the Dk.OpamLock hermetic bootstrap (opam detects MSYS2 via
usr/bin/cygpath.exe). Windows x86_64 only: x86/arm64 Windows hosts run the
x64 tree through WOW64/emulation.

  $ get-object CommonsLang_OCaml.MSYS2@2026.6.11 -s Release.Windows_x86_64 -f ${RUNTIME}/Windows_x86_64-MSYS2-2026.6.11.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "ozjqpoyewgl2wsnrk5uekbleo3644auhcyri2gexstfr3k5slof5q")\;

## Dk.OpamLock

  $ run-function CommonsLang_OCaml.Dk.OpamLock.Export@1.0.0 -f ${RUNTIME}/OpamLock.Export.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "o4z5z3zdrecgprn5m46h7hczhygs6tra4jc4tjxwtfdqxagnsik2a")\;

The @1.1.0 revision ships alongside @1.0.0: its Solve rule delegates the lock
logic to a compiled OCaml helper (dk_opam_lock.ml + a vendored opam-file-format
amalgam), fixing the lua-ml depends-order scramble and the dropped
Linux_x86_64_musl slot. @1.1.0 is a fresh id, so it builds clean.

  $ run-function CommonsLang_OCaml.Dk.OpamLock.Export@1.1.0 -f ${RUNTIME}/OpamLock.Export-1.1.0.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "ook3wmaqxmmt4j2ctuuh44dx2h34nv4rdmzdjfuafmdepnxjlkc7a")\;
  $ run-function CommonsLang_OCaml.Dk.OpamLock.Export@1.1.1 -f ${RUNTIME}/OpamLock.Export-1.1.1.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "oxagrq3htmsekhfb3f2ulnmrburpbycp4e7rktb4g7lts4jfuxnbq")\;
  $ run-function CommonsLang_OCaml.Dk.OpamLock.Export@1.1.3 -f ${RUNTIME}/OpamLock.Export-1.1.3.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "oungtccyisk2xvxutd66iipg4dgx2gx5u2ancalwwbfd4vt7t5y4a")\;
  $ run-function CommonsLang_OCaml.Dk.OpamLock.Export@1.1.4 -f ${RUNTIME}/OpamLock.Export-1.1.4.zip
  \test(pass)
  \dk.object(abi: "Release.Windows_x86_64", value-id: "oungtccyisk2xvxutd66iipg4dgx2gx5u2ancalwwbfd4vt7t5y4a")\;


